    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **55 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe customer-code assignment in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` previously set the raw computed code (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`) directly. I added de-duplication so a collision with an existing owner's `customerCode` gets a `-<n>` suffix using the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n**At the assignment site** (owner create):\n```java\nowner.setCustomerCode(deduplicateCustomerCode(customerCode(\n    deriveRegion(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity()), normalizedTelephone, owner.getLastName())));\n```\n\n**New helper** (next to the existing `customerCode`/`hash8` methods):\n```java\nprivate String deduplicateCustomerCode(String base) {\n    Set<String> inUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n        .map(Owner::getCustomerCode)\n        .filter(Objects::nonNull)\n        .collect(Collectors.toSet());\n    if (!inUse.contains(base)) {\n        return base;\n    }\n    int n = 2;\n    while (inUse.contains(base + \"-\" + n)) {\n        n++;\n    }\n    return base + \"-\" + n;\n}\n```\n\nIt returns the base code unchanged when free; otherwise it scans existing owners' codes and appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 choosing the smallest suffix not already in use \u2014 returning the de-duplicated `customerCode`. The new `Cp41Tests` (distinct owners get distinct codes) and all other customer-code tests pass.",
